# L §2.2 (writer 8): in_force is gone from the built-ins; L §4.3 "A commencement that rules test ... is a row of its
# own, and every rule that tests it reads that row". A call takes a built-in's name or a band's id (L §2.3 Calls):
# in_force(...) names no band, LOAD-NAME.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

def relief: int at reader
  rule base = 0

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026-07..
  known 2026-06-01
  replace rule relief.extra beats base = 1

ask q1: in_force(relief.extra, 2026-03-01), in_force(relief.extra, 2026-08-01), in_force(relief.base, 2026-03-01)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-NAME ...
